Ported from Redis 7.2.16: BSD 3-Clause License, Copyright (c) 2006-2020,
Salvatore Sanfilippo, and the authors named in its files. Where Redis 7.2
answers otherwise than 7.0, BendKV answers as Redis 7.2.16 does, and these
parts of it are written from 7.2.16's sources:

- Tools: tools/redis_ref.sh, which builds Redis 7.2.16 from its tarball
  for the tests to compare with (nothing of Redis is kept here).
- Tables: tools/data/redis-commands.json, COMMAND INFO and COMMAND DOCS of
  Redis 7.2.16's commands (from src/commands/*.json, as a running server
  answers them), and the tables tools/gen_commands.py writes from it into
  src/command.bend, src/acl.bend and src/redis.bend.
- Texts and fields: the HELP replies, CLIENT LIST's fields (networking.c),
  INFO's fields and their order, its listeners and its debug section
  (server.c, connection.c), LOLWUT's line, and the version HELLO, INFO and
  Lua's redis.REDIS_VERSION give (src/redis.bend, src/info.bend,
  src/session.bend, src/lua/engine.c).
- Scripts: src/lua/engine.c, from script_lua.c, eval.c and function_lua.c
  (the deprecated builtins and lua-enable-deprecated-api, the protection
  of the basic types' metatables of CVE-2025-46818, redis.set_repl()'s
  and redis.acl_check_cmd()'s checks, math.random outside a run, an
  error's text on one line); src/server.bend, from script.c (a call's
  ACL failure) and script_lua.c (SCRIPT KILL's line in the log); and
  src/rdb.bend, from functions.c (FUNCTION RESTORE of the pre-GA format).
- Blocked calls: a call that blocks counted when its client is unblocked
  (served, its time up, or by CLIENT UNBLOCK), not when it blocks, and
  never when its client goes while it waits but in WAIT (blocked.c's
  updateStatsOnUnblock, server.c's call() and replication.c), in
  src/info.bend and src/server.bend.
- Configuration: tools/data/redis-configs.json, the parameters of
  Redis 7.2.16's config.c, and the table tools/gen_config.py writes from
  it into src/config.bend; the checks of cluster-announce-ip,
  cluster-announce-human-nodename and locale-collate, as config.c's
  isValidClusterAnnounceIp, cluster.c's isValidAuxChar and config.c's
  updateLocaleCollate make them (src/config.bend, src/server.bend), and
  loglevel's nothing (src/startup.bend).
- Start and shutdown: the levels and texts of their lines in the log
  (server.c's main and prepareForShutdown, and the listeners of socket.c
  and unix.c), in src/server.bend.
- Persistence: src/rdb.bend, from rdb.c, t_set.c and t_stream.c (RDB
  version 11: sets as SET_LISTPACK, the order an intset's members take
  when a set read from a file becomes a listpack, streams as
  STREAM_LISTPACKS_3 with each consumer's active time, the formats of
  7.0's and 4.0's release candidates refused); src/server.bend, from
  rdb.c and server.c (the lines of a file that does not load or open, of
  a save's write error and of a directory's sync).
- Texts and checks: HELLO's order (networking.c's helloCommand: every
  option read before any is done, then the last AUTH, NOAUTH's text, the
  name and the protocol), NOPERM's texts and ACL DRYRUN's (acl.c's
  getAclErrorMessage), XREAD's text for unbalanced streams and XSETID's
  check against the greatest ID deleted (t_stream.c), and LPOS's range
  for RANK (t_list.c), in src/session.bend, src/acl.bend,
  src/server.bend and src/redis.bend.
- ACL LOG's entry-id, timestamp-created and timestamp-last-updated, and
  the count of entries made, which ACL LOG RESET keeps (acl.c), in
  src/acl.bend.
- Doubles: src/float.bend's f64.dtoa, ported from fpconv_dtoa.c and
  fpconv_powers.h (Grisu2, under the Boost Software License 1.0 as
  above), and its f64.show, from util.c's d2string and double2ll; and
  which of them Redis writes a double with where (networking.c's
  addReplyDouble, t_zset.c's zzlInsertAt, rio.c's rioWriteBulkDouble,
  db.c's scan of a sorted set), in src/redis.bend, src/rdb.bend,
  src/aof.bend, src/acl.bend and src/info.bend; and d2string and
  double2ll in tests/float_ref.c.
- XINFO STREAM FULL's active-time and XINFO CONSUMERS' inactive
  (t_stream.c), in src/redis.bend and src/stream.bend.

